  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Maya, you're verified. I checked order O-5101 from Pho Real. It was promised by 6:40 PM and arrived at 7:05 PM, which is 25 minutes late.\n\nI've added **$3.99** in account credit, equal to your delivery fee, to your account. You can use it on a future order.\n\nOur policy doesn't cover compensation for food that arrives lukewarm, so I can't offer anything extra for the pho. If the food made you ill, or if an item was missing or wrong, tell me and I'll look into it.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I don't want account credit. I'd like the money back on my Visa, the card I paid with. $3.99 is nothing for a 25 minute wait on a dinner I was looking forward to after a long shift."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I'm sorry, Maya. I know a late dinner after a long shift is frustrating. Our policy only allows account credit for late deliveries, not a refund to your card. For a delivery 25 minutes late, the credit is the delivery fee, which is $3.99. I can't change either of those.\n\nThe $3.99 credit is on your account and will apply to a future order. I can also pass your feedback to a specialist if you'd like. They would follow up within 24 hours, but I can't promise a different outcome.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok. Pushing back once was my shot, so I'll take the credit. Please pass the feedback along, though. Getting it 25 minutes late and lukewarm after a shift like today is rough."
  },
